\begin{align*}
\text{Number of red cards with caution} &= \text{Number of players with caution} \times 2 \\
&= 5 \times 2 = 10 \, \text{yellow cards} &\text{(because each red card corresponds to } 2 \, \text{yellow cards)}\\
\end{align*}
Now, to find the total number of red cards the whole team would collect, we need to divide the number of yellow cards with caution by 2:
\begin{align*}
\text{Total number of red cards} &= \frac{\text{Number of yellow cards with caution}}{2}\\
&= \frac{10}{2} = 5 \,\boxed{\text{red cards}}} \\
\end{align*}
So, the whole team would collect \boxed{5} red cards. 
